From f9e987583537f387a5afe6c26c125a6701d592b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 13:02:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Close the loop between check-in, Today and Explore

Six additions, all on top of the existing shell:

- Today now reads the most recent check-in and says plainly why it
  reordered "meet the day where it is" (e.g. "you said foggy, and
  nothing yet today"). Nothing is hidden, the order just responds.
- Explore gets a barrier filter (decision-load, sensory-load,
  activation, shame, time-blindness, words) alongside the existing
  pillar filter, backed by a new `barriers` field on every lived
  moment card.
- Every card carries a small effort-dot cue (1-3, derived from its
  duration) so a 3-minute and a 10-minute moment don't read the same
  at a glance.
- Cards with a genuine source behind them (not all of them) carry a
  "Cited" badge that jumps straight to the matching entry in the
  evidence register in More, instead of leaving it three taps away.
- A low-stimulation mode toggle on Today mutes colour and disables
  motion app-wide (state.settings.lowStimulation), for when sensory
  load is the barrier the check-in just named.
- My plan gains a six-pillar strip extending the existing eating-
  rhythm pattern (opportunities, not commands) to Begin, Regulate,
  Connect, Move and Understand, not just Nourish.

Verified: lint, typecheck (pre-existing beta/smoke worker errors
unrelated to this change), unit tests, production build, and the
axe-core rendered accessibility suite all pass unchanged.

